From: VLCDotNet CI <ci@vlcdotnet>
Subject: [PATCH] contrib: build libass with DirectWrite on desktop Windows

VLC's contrib only switches libass to the native DirectWrite font provider for
WinStore/UWP targets; regular desktop Win32 still pulls in `fontconfig` and
`libxml2`. libass 0.17.3 supports DirectWrite on desktop Windows too, so treat
`HAVE_WIN32` like `HAVE_WINSTORE`: disable fontconfig and enable DirectWrite.
Linux, which has no `HAVE_WIN32`, keeps fontconfig unchanged.
---
 contrib/src/ass/rules.mak | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/contrib/src/ass/rules.mak b/contrib/src/ass/rules.mak
index 4171273..3d65e50 100644
--- a/contrib/src/ass/rules.mak
+++ b/contrib/src/ass/rules.mak
@@ -20,7 +20,9 @@ else
 ifdef HAVE_DARWIN_OS
 WITH_FONTCONFIG = 0
 else
-ifdef HAVE_WINSTORE
+# Desktop Windows uses libass' native DirectWrite font provider (like UWP),
+# avoiding fontconfig and its libxml2 dependency.
+ifdef HAVE_WIN32
 WITH_FONTCONFIG = 0
 WITH_DWRITE = 1
 else
